  "statement": "The derived unconstrained flow of the one-loop quadratic V(h, y) has a unique stable hidden critical point at the origin, where r is a flat (neutrally stable) direction. Linear T on 4_3 \u2295 4_5 \u2295 H13 is independent of r (Yukawas are cubic; the hidden-source Jacobian at zero vanishes). The cycle-17 convergence law slaves \u03b4(t) to the input \u03b4* and does not select r: sample trajectories with the time-dependent H5(t) still collapse to h = 0 at distinct final ratios. Constraining |h| = 1 is extra; it places the vev on the lighter hidden quartet without fixing r. Minimising the bubble-chain spectral radius on the Yukawa sphere is extra and gives r_* = 0.00292218 (\u2248 \u221a(\u03c0_o/\u03c0_e) \u221a(H5/H3)), not a derivation. Uncoupled T0 poles remain z1, z2 of cycle 05, independent of r. No unique stable fixed point selects r."
